  (may contain items - view "/Student_People" to load from database)
  ↪ To append: action "add" at "/Student_People" with value.
• /Student_Interests (array, 4 items) — Things the student enjoys or is interested in 
  - [0]: "facts"
  - [1]: "drawing"
  - [2]: "music"
  - [3]: "science"
  ↪ To append: action "add" at "/Student_Interests" with value. To update item: action "set" at "/Student_Interests/<index>".
• /Student_CommunicationStyle (object) — How the student communicates (method only, not detailed abilities) 
  - PrimaryMethod: "AAC" — verbal, nonverbal, AAC, or mixed
  - PreferredModality: <string> — If AAC, which type (symbols, text, combined) (empty)
  ↪ To expand: view "/Student_CommunicationStyle/*". To modify: action "set" on "/Student_CommunicationStyle" or "/Student_CommunicationStyle/<property>".
• /Student_Preferences (object) — Student's preferences for activities, rewards, and engagement 
  - FavoriteActivities: {array} (hidden)
  - RewardPreferences: {array} (empty)
  - AvoidTopics: {array} — Topics that should be avoided in conversation (empty)
  ↪ To expand: view "/Student_Preferences/*". To modify: action "set" on "/Student_Preferences" or "/Student_Preferences/<property>".
• /Student_Notes (array, 1 items) — General notes about the student (non-sensitive) 
  - [0]: "Gal strongly prefers interactive apps (drawing, music) over passive activities and consistently chooses the iPad as his device of choice. He engages well with 'Facts' and 'Science' interests through hands-on exploration (experiments, how things work, chemistry, weather) and farm games."
  ↪ To append: action "add" at "/Student_Notes" with value. To update item: action "set" at "/Student_Notes/<index>".
• /Context_Library (map, 0 keys) — Knowledge base topics organized hierarchically. Browse by viewing topics and their subtopics. Each topic may contain educational content and/or nested subtopics. 
  (may contain items - view "/Context_Library" to load from database)
• /Context_StudentInfo (object) — Basic information about the student (name, age, language, etc.) 
  ↪ To expand: view "/Context_StudentInfo/*". (read-only)
• /Context_StudentInstitutes (array, 0 items) — Schools and clinics the student attends — hidden; view to list items
• /Context_Classes (array, 0 items) — Classes the student is enrolled in — hidden; view to list items
• /Context_Classmates (array, 0 items) — Other students and staff in the student's classes — hidden; view to list items
• /Context_MedicalInfo (object) — Medical records and health information (read-only) — hidden; view to list keys
• /Context_FunctionalInfo (object) — Functional assessment reports (read-only) — hidden; view to list keys
• /Context_EducationalInfo (object) — Educational reports and accommodations (read-only) — hidden; view to list keys
• /Context_Progress (object) — Current IEP/program goals and progress (read-only) 
  ↪ To expand: view "/Context_Progress/*". (read-only)
• /Context_AACPrompt (object) — The custom prompt that guides the Interactive Agent's behavior during AAC sessions. Update this when student goals, medical info, or context changes. 
  - prompt: <string> — The full custom prompt text (empty)
  ↪ To expand: view "/Context_AACPrompt/*". To modify: action "set" on "/Context_AACPrompt" or "/Context_AACPrompt/<property>".
• /Context_AACSettings (object) — Configuration for the AAC system — voice, display, input, symbols, privacy, and apps — hidden; view to list keys

Allowed roots & types: /Student_People{array}, /Student_Interests{array}, /Student_CommunicationStyle{object}, /Student_Preferences{object}, /Student_Notes{array}, /Context_Library{map}, /Context_StudentInfo{object}, /Context_StudentInstitutes{array}, /Context_Classes{array}, /Context_Classmates{array}, /Context_MedicalInfo{object}, /Context_FunctionalInfo{object}, /Context_EducationalInfo{object}, /Context_Progress{object}, /Context_AACPrompt{object}, /Context_AACSettings{object}
Operate only on visible paths or their parent container. To reveal children:
  manageMemory { "ops": [ { "action": "view", "path": "/path/*" } ] }
Pagination: include { "page": { "offset": N, "limit": M } } in a view op on a container.

=== Schema Hints (add/insert/upsert in current scope) ===
• /Student_People — ARRAY of object
  item.required: [Name]
  item.props: Name:string, Relationship:string
  e.g. add → manageMemory { "ops":[{ "action":"add","path":"/Student_People","value": {"Name":"text"} }] }
• /Student_Interests — ARRAY of string
  e.g. add → manageMemory { "ops":[{ "action":"add","path":"/Student_Interests","value": "text" }] }
• /Student_Preferences/FavoriteActivities — ARRAY of string
  e.g. add → manageMemory { "ops":[{ "action":"add","path":"/Student_Preferences/FavoriteActivities","value": "text" }] }
• /Student_Preferences/RewardPreferences — ARRAY of string
  e.g. add → manageMemory { "ops":[{ "action":"add","path":"/Student_Preferences/RewardPreferences","value": "text" }] }
• /Student_Preferences/AvoidTopics — ARRAY of string
  e.g. add → manageMemory { "ops":[{ "action":"add","path":"/Student_Preferences/AvoidTopics","value": "text" }] }
• /Student_Notes — ARRAY of string
  e.g. add → manageMemory { "ops":[{ "action":"add","path":"/Student_Notes","value": "text" }] }
• /Context_Library — MAP<string, object>
  value.props: id:string, title:string, content:string, subtopics:map<string, object>
  e.g. add → manageMemory { "ops":[{ "action":"add","path":"/Context_Library","key":"<key>","value": {} }] }

Notes:
- When item/value is an OBJECT, include all listed "required" keys when creating it.
- Arrays/maps may enforce limits (uniqueItems, min/max counts) and map keys may have regex constraints.
- For topics, "value" may be a string (description) or a full node {description?, subtopics?}.
